.TH CCOL_CIRCQ_TRY_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_circq_try_recv_zc \- try to receive a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_circq_try_recv_zc(ccol_circular_queue *cq,
                                 c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Takes a message from the queue if one is there, and returns
ccol_container_empty at once when the queue is empty. The data is
handed over without a copy.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq          Circular queue to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - A message was received. The caller must free
                       target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args    - cq or target_buf is NULL
ccol_container_empty - The queue is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This call never blocks. After a successful call the data belongs to
the caller, who must free target_buf->data.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_circq_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_circq_timed_recv_zc (3)
